    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342-a2">

                <pb facs="0486" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg406"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibson to Mr. Smith.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-10-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                    1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of even date, informing me of the death of President William
                    McKinley, information of which has this day reached you. In reply I have to say
                    that my Government sincerely and deeply regret that the President of the United
                    States should have come to an untimely grave by the hand of a ruthless assassin,
                    and as a nation we deeply sympathize with the American nation, our foster
                    mother.</p>
                <p>With sentiments of the deepest sympathy, I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. V. Gibson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
